---
import '@fontsource/inter/400.css';
import '@fontsource/inter/500.css';
import '@fontsource/inter/600.css';
import '@fontsource/inter/700.css';
import '../styles/global.css';
import { yearsLabel } from '../lib/experience.js';

const experience = yearsLabel();
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Carlos Enrique Piñeiro — Software Engineer</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Carlos Enrique Piñeiro is a software engineer in Santa Clara, Cuba, building end-to-end as an AI-augmented developer. Solo developer of Carlito, a native Android utility hub for daily life in Cuba."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="wrap">
      <header>
        <h1>Carlos Enrique Piñeiro</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Software Engineer — Santa Clara, Cuba</p>
        <p class="contact">
          <a href="mailto:carlosepc.com@gmail.com">carlosepc.com@gmail.com</a>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <a href="https://github.com/carlosepcc">github.com/carlosepcc</a>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <a href="https://x.com/carlosepcc">x.com/carlosepcc</a>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <a href="https://hive.blog/@carlosepc">hive.blog/@carlosepc</a>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <a href="tel:+5355062672">+53 5506 2672</a>
        </p>
        <div class="cv-buttons">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/cv.pdf" download>Download CV (PDF)</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/cv.md" download>Download CV (Markdown)</a>
        </div>
        <p class="cv-note">
          Both files are generated from the same source and updated together.
        </p>
      </header>

      <main>
        <section id="summary">
          <h2>Summary</h2>
          <p>
            Software engineer with deep frontend expertise and a product
            mindset, now building end-to-end as an AI-augmented developer.
            {experience} of development experience, starting with Vue and
            Quasar on university projects and my thesis in 2020: shipping web
            products for international clients (Vue/Nuxt ecosystem), backend
            architecture remediation with Node.js/ExpressJS,
            Prisma and Zod, and two years teaching AI/ML at the University of
            Computer Sciences (UCI). Currently proving the next step in public:
            <strong>Carlito</strong>, a native Android app I&rsquo;m designing,
            architecting, and developing solo — it started as a Google AI
            Studio experiment to organize my PAGOxMÓVIL SMS and grew into a
            full utility hub — learning the Android platform along the way,
            with AI tools handling the tedious work while I keep every
            technical decision.
          </p>
          <p>
            I work best with autonomy: I take a problem from first principles
            to a shipped product, prepare context carefully, split work
            sensibly, direct tools (human or AI), and verify every result.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="skills">
          <h2>Technical skills</h2>
          <div class="skill-group">
            <span class="label">Solid</span>
            <ul>
              <li>Languages: JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML, CSS (SASS/SCSS)</li>
              <li>
                Frontend: Vue 3, Nuxt, TailwindCSS, Quasar, React / Next.js
              </li>
              <li>
                Backend: Node.js, ExpressJS, Prisma, Zod (validation, API
                architecture remediation)
              </li>
              <li>
                UI/UX implementation: Material 3 / Material You, design
                systems, Figma
              </li>
              <li>
                Workflow: Git, GitHub (issues, branching, conventional
                commits), Agile teams, Jira
              </li>
              <li>Integration: REST APIs, LDAP, Supabase</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="skill-group">
            <span class="label">Developing</span>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Android native: Kotlin, Jetpack Compose (building Carlito and
                Meco — in beta)
              </li>
              <li>
                Telephony/SMS integration: USSD flows, SMS parsing, biometric
                authentication
              </li>
              <li>
                TanStack Start + Chakra UI v3 (Hivepen Studio), Astro
                (hivepen.com)
              </li>
              <li>Python for AI/ML teaching (Google Colab)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="skill-group">
            <span class="label">Currently learning</span>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Android platform depth — learning through building and
                shipping Carlito and Meco
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <p>
            <strong>Strengths:</strong> product thinking, client
            communication, technical demos and presentations, mentoring.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="carlito">
          <h2>Featured project</h2>
          <h3>
            Carlito — native Android utility hub for daily life in Cuba
            <span class="status">In beta · sole developer</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="meta">Android (Kotlin, Jetpack Compose)</p>
          <p>
            I own everything: product vision, architecture, UI, and code. It
            started as an experiment to organize PAGOxMÓVIL banking SMS and
            grew into a full utility hub for Cuban mobile services.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Pizarra:</strong> ETECSA balance dashboard (main balance,
              data, voice, bonuses, SMS) with validity dates, queried over
              USSD.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Banca:</strong> BPA bank accounts with biometric-protected
              PIN storage, transfers and online payments (Pago en Línea).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Mensajes:</strong> inbox organized by sender (ETECSA,
              ENZONA, Nauta, CUBACEL) instead of a chronological dump.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Architecture documented as living docs alongside the code
            (roadmaps for USSD encoding, dual-SIM, online payments, UI
            modularization). A Flutter migration is in progress. Coming next:
            Nauta Hogar.
          </p>
          <p class="project-links">
            Published on Apklis (315 CUP) and Zapstore ·
            <a href="https://hivepen.com/apps/carlito/get/apklis">Apklis</a>
            <a href="https://hivepen.com/apps/carlito/get/zapstore">Zapstore</a>
            <a href="https://cucoders.dev/apps/carlosepcc/carlito/">CuCoders</a>
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="projects">
          <h2>More projects</h2>
          <h3>Meco</h3>
          <p>
            Android client for Nauta Hogar (ETECSA), rebuilt from the
            open-source NautaPy CLI tool. Minimalist design inspired by clean
            smart-home apps. Planned open-source.
          </p>
          <h3>
            Miazucar <span class="status">Client work</span>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Flutter app built on commission for a home baker: it calculates
            ingredient costs per product unit, with a personalised price
            factor. Signed Android release delivered to the client.
          </p>
          <h3>
            Hivepen Studio
            <span class="status">studio.hivepen.com · in development</span>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Advanced workspace for Hive creators, communities, and curators.
            TanStack Start + Chakra UI v3.
          </p>
          <h3>
            Genioo
            <span class="status">genioo.hivepen.com · in development</span>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Brain-training games that reward focus and logic. No ads.
          </p>
          <h3>
            Gloti <span class="status">Prototype</span>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Language learning through stories, in real context. Being migrated
            to a hivepen.com subdomain.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="experience">
          <h2>Experience</h2>
          <h3>Backend Developer (contract) — Independent client, US-based</h3>
          <p class="meta">Remote · Jan 2026 – Feb 2026</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Remediated backend architecture in ExpressJS + Prisma projects:
              introduced Zod validation and improved scalability and
              maintainability of backend–frontend integration.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Frontend Developer — DaraServices</h3>
          <p class="meta">Remote, Mexico · Jan 2025 – Jun 2025</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Built B2B collaboration modules with Vue, TypeScript, and
              Tailwind.
            </li>
            <li>
              Worked directly with product teams to present UX solutions to
              clients.
            </li>
            <li>
              Led knowledge-sharing sessions on Material You design
              implementation.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Frontend Developer (AI &amp; E-Commerce) — NataSquad</h3>
          <p class="meta">Remote, France · Apr 2023 – Sep 2024</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Led frontend development for AI e-commerce services with Nuxt.
            </li>
            <li>
              Presented technical demos to investors and client stakeholders.
            </li>
            <li>
              Integrated UX prototyping (Figma), SEO optimization, and AI
              image-generation features.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Frontend Web Developer — JadeTech Group</h3>
          <p class="meta">Havana, Cuba · Nov 2023 – Feb 2024</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Implemented e-commerce platforms while engaging directly with
              clients on feature requirements.
            </li>
            <li>
              Presented technical solutions to cross-functional teams in
              sprint reviews.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <h3>
            AI/ML Teaching Assistant &amp; Lecturer — University of Computer
            Sciences (UCI)
          </h3>
          <p class="meta">Havana, Cuba · Feb 2023 – Jul 2025</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Taught AI/ML concepts to 200+ students through lectures and
              workshops.
            </li>
            <li>
              Delivered conference-style presentations on emerging AI trends.
            </li>
            <li>
              Built course materials bridging theory with practical
              engineering (Python, Google Colab).
            </li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Institutional systems — CDIS</h3>
          <p class="meta">University of Computer Sciences (UCI)</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Designed and implemented the frontend of a disciplinary-process
              management system (Vue 3, Quasar, TypeScript) with role-based
              access, LDAP integration, and real-time reporting; trained 50+
              administrative staff.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="education">
          <h2>Education</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>B.S. in Computer Science (Software Engineering focus)</strong>
            — University of Computer Sciences (UCI), Havana, Cuba · 2017 – 2022
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="languages">
          <h2>Languages</h2>
          <p>
            Spanish — native<br />
            English — C1 Proficient · EF SET Certification
          </p>
        </section>
      </main>

      <footer>
        <p>
          The fastest way to reach me is email:
          <a href="mailto:carlosepc.com@gmail.com">carlosepc.com@gmail.com</a>.
          My CV is always available here as
          <a href="/cv.pdf">PDF</a> or <a href="/cv.md">Markdown</a>.
        </p>
        <p>Carlos Enrique Piñeiro · Santa Clara, Cuba · November 2026</p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
